[{"content":"You can call these tools (parameters are JSON Schema; \"required\" lists the required arguments, and \"default\" is the value used when an optional argument is left out):\n\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cancel_order\",\n    \"description\": \"Cancel a store order that has not been delivered yet and refund it to the chosen payment method.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"order_id\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Store order id, formatted like 'ORD-123456'.\"\n        },\n        \"reason\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Why the customer is cancelling, used for reporting.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"changed_mind\",\n            \"found_cheaper\",\n            \"ordered_by_mistake\",\n            \"arrives_too_late\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"refund_method\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Where the refund is paid: the original card or store credit.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"original_payment\",\n            \"store_credit\"\n          ],\n          \"default\": \"original_payment\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"order_id\",\n        \"reason\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"kube.scale_deployment\",\n    \"description\": \"Set the number of replicas of a Kubernetes deployment; the cluster adds or removes pods to match.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"deployment\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Name of the deployment, exactly as given, e.g. 'checkout-api'.\"\n        },\n        \"replicas\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"Desired number of replicas, from 0 to 50.\"\n        },\n        \"namespace\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Kubernetes namespace the resource lives in.\",\n          \"default\": \"default\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"deployment\",\n        \"replicas\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"calendar.delete_event\",\n    \"description\": \"Delete one event from the calendar by its id; attendees can be told that it was cancelled.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"event_id\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Event id exactly as returned by calendar.list_events, e.g. 'evt_3k9w'.\"\n        },\n        \"notify_attendees\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"description\": \"Email the attendees a cancellation notice.\",\n          \"default\": true\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"event_id\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"calendar.list_events\",\n    \"description\": \"List the events on one day of a calendar, with their ids, titles, start times and attendees.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"date\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"The day to list, formatted as YYYY-MM-DD, in the calendar's time zone.\"\n        },\n        \"calendar_id\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Which calendar to read; 'primary' is the user's own calendar.\",\n          \"default\": \"primary\"\n        },\n        \"include_declined\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\",\n          \"description\": \"Also list events the user has declined.\",\n          \"default\": false\n        },\n        \"max_results\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"Maximum number of events to return, earliest first.\",\n          \"default\": 50\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"date\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"calendar.create_event\",\n    \"description\": \"Create a new event on the user's primary calendar and send invitations to any attendees listed.\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"title\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Short title shown on the calendar, e.g. 'Design review'.\"\n        },\n        \"start\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Local start date and time of the event, formatted as YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM.\"\n        },\n        \"duration_minutes\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"Length of the event in minutes; the calendar default is half an hour.\",\n          \"default\": 30\n        },\n        \"attendees\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"description\": \"Email addresses of the people to invite, in any order.\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Email address\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"location\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Room name or address where the event takes place, as free text.\"\n        },\n        \"reminder_minutes\": {\n          \"type\": \"integer\",\n          \"description\": \"Minutes before the start at which to send a reminder notification.\",\n          \"default\": 10\n        },\n        \"visibility\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"description\": \"Who can see the event details on shared calendars.\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"default\",\n            \"public\",\n            \"private\"\n          ],\n          \"default\": \"default\"\n        },\n        \"recurrence\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"description\": \"Repeat rule for a recurring event; a one-off event when left out.\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"frequency\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"description\": \"How often the event repeats.\",\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"daily\",\n                \"weekly\",\n                \"monthly\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"count\": {\n              \"type\": \"integer\",\n              \"description\": \"Total number of occurrences, the first one included.\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"frequency\",\n            \"count\"\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"title\",\n        \"start\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: What's on my calendar on 2026-08-12?\n\nReply with only a JSON array of the tool calls that fulfil the request, each of the form {\"name\": \"<tool name>\", \"arguments\": {...}}, where \"arguments\" is a JSON object (not a string). When the request needs several calls, list them all. Reply with [] if no tool fits the request, or if the request does not give a value for a required argument: never guess one. Include every required argument. Include an optional argument only if the request asks for a value for it; otherwise leave it out and the tool applies its default. Give each value the type its schema declares: JSON numbers for integer and number, true or false for boolean, and strings for string, copied exactly as written.","role":"user"},{"content":"[{\"name\":\"calendar.list_events\",\"arguments\":{\"date\":\"2026-08-12\"}}]","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool results:\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"calendar.list_events\",\n    \"result\": [\n      {\n        \"event_id\": \"evt_9100a\",\n        \"title\": \"Design review\",\n        \"start\": \"2026-08-12T09:30\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"event_id\": \"evt_3553b\",\n        \"title\": \"Team lunch\",\n        \"start\": \"2026-08-12T13:00\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"event_id\": \"evt_1120c\",\n        \"title\": \"Vendor call\",\n        \"start\": \"2026-08-12T15:30\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n\nRequest: Cancel the Design review without notifying anyone.\n\nReply as before: only a JSON array of tool calls, or [] if no tool fits o